<title>USA: PacifiCorp Centralia power plant back up.</title>
<headline>PacifiCorp Centralia power plant back up.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 670-megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the Centralia power plant in southwest Washington state was restarted Monday afternoon, said a spokesman for PacifiCorp on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The coal-fired unit was shut Saturday afternoon for repairs to a boiler tube leak.</p>
<p>Centralia's other 670-MW unit tripped off due to a similar problem on Thursday and was back on-line Saturday morning.</p>
<p>PacifiCorp owns a 47.5 percent stake in Centralia and operates the plant.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau, + 1 213 955 6761</p>
